{"id": "85981", "name": "נגזרת של aˣ·xᵃ – מכפלה עם מעריכית (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Find the following derivative:</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\( \\displaystyle \\frac{d}{d{{CT:0}}}({{CT:1}}) = \\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Applying the product rule</b><br>The simplest way to solve this problem is using the product rule.<div style=\"background:#FFF8E6;border:1px solid #E8D29A;border-radius:10px;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0\">The product rule: \\( \\frac{d}{dx}(uv)=u'v+uv' \\)</div>Define \\(f={{CT:2}}\\) and \\(g={{CT:3}}\\) so that \\(f'=\\log({{CT:4}}){{CT:2}}\\) and \\(g'={{CT:4}}{{CT:0}}^{{CT:5}}\\). So,<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\begin{array}{rcl} \\displaystyle \\frac{d}{d{{CT:0}}}({{CT:1}}) &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle f\\cdot g' + f'\\cdot g \\\\ &\\displaystyle =&\\displaystyle {{CT:2}} \\cdot {{CT:4}}{{CT:0}}^{{CT:5}} + {{CT:6}} \\\\ & =&\\displaystyle {{CT:7}}. \\end{array} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>",